    {
      "bbox": [
        594,
        627,
        1817,
        1109
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "A constructive idea has begun to take hold all over Manhattan. Since the rush hour congestion in transportation is largely caused by the 9 to 5 work habit, with most people coming and going at the same hours, why not judiciously shift the work hours a bit? Stagger the times of arrival and departure. What's so holy about 9 to 5?",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.3993,
          "min": -2.0849
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0002
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 75,
          "mean": -0.0088,
          "min": -0.6145
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 5480,
        "area_px": 593124,
        "density": 0.00924,
        "chars": 329,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 60.04
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        333,
        1113,
        1817,
        1421
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "If this were done, the peak hours would thus be spread out. Some people would start a little earlier and leave earlier. Others might arrive later and depart later. And they could certainly expect to ride in greater comfort on their transportation systems, with a better chance for a seat.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.3359,
          "min": -1.9239
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 56,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0012
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 2692,
        "area_px": 458920,
        "density": 0.00587,
        "chars": 288,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 106.98
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        329,
        1419,
        1817,
        2040
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The Staggered Work Hours Program began in lower Manhattan. In April, 1970, about 50,000 men and women from 45 private firms and government agencies in the downtown area began a new program of staggered work hours designed to determine in hard fact whether a shifting away from the traditional 9 to 5 schedule would relieve transportation congestion. This new program was and is jointly sponsored by the Downtown-Lower Manhattan Association and The Port of New York Authority.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2987,
          "min": -1.3247
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 101,
          "mean": -0.0014,
          "min": -0.1302
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 5078,
        "area_px": 927774,
        "density": 0.00547,
        "chars": 475,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 93.54
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        325,
        2036,
        1377,
        2725
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "By September, 1971, the program had more than 70,000 individuals participating from 116 firms and public agencies in the lower Manhattan community, including the banking, insurance and investment industries, corporate headquarters groups, the State and City of New York and the Federal Government. The shifts from 9 to 5 hours were principally to a new schedule from 8:30 to 4:30 although many also switched to 9:30 to 5:30.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.3464,
          "min": -1.7289
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 107,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0027
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 5003,
        "area_px": 727584,
        "density": 0.00688,
        "chars": 424,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 84.75
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        325,
        2725,
        1355,
        2982
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The operations of Staggered Work Hours have been intensively assessed and analyzed. The verdict is overwhelmingly favorable.",
